  "explanation": {
    "id": "ec5e44b4-580d-408d-8859-7589279accb6",
    "body": "Hint: Use the multivariable chain rule formula: $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t} = \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t} + \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t} + \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}$. You are given all the numerical values you need; you just need to compute the partial derivatives of $f$ first.",
